{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Mariaan de Swardt (born 18 March 1971) is a former tennis player from South Africa, who played as a professional from 1988 to 2001.","title":"Mariaan de Swardt"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She twice represented her native country at the Summer Olympics, in 1992 and 1996, and was a member of the South African Fed Cup Team in 1992 and 1994–1997.","title":"Mariaan de Swardt"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 2006, de Swardt became a U.S. citizen.","title":"Mariaan de Swardt"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 1999 Wimbledon Championships – Women's Doubles was the women's doubles event of the hundred-and-thirteenth edition of Wimbledon, the third Grand Slam of the year, the most prestigious tournament on grass courts, and the oldest tennis tournament in the world.","title":"1999 Wimbledon Championships – Women's Doubles"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Martina Hingis and Jana Novotná were the defending champions but only Novotná competed that year with Natasha Zvereva.","title":"1999 Wimbledon Championships – Women's Doubles"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Novotná and Zvereva lost in the semifinals to Mariaan de Swardt and Elena Tatarkova.","title":"1999 Wimbledon Championships – Women's Doubles"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Serena Williams has won dozens of Grand Slam singles titles, multiple Olympic gold medals, held the world No. 1 ranking and completed a Career Doubles Grand Slam, whereas Mariaan de Swardt is only noted as a doubles finalist at the 1998 Boston Cup.
